## IBrowserService

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Contracts`
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Components.Core`

### Purpose
Opens new browser windows/tabs for URIs, files, or raw HTML content. Provides window lifecycle management via `IWindowHandle`.

### Interface Definition

```csharp
public interface IBrowserService : IDisposable
{
    IWindowHandle OpenUri(Uri uri, string title = "Cyréna");
    IWindowHandle OpenFile(string filePath, string title = "Cyréna");
    IWindowHandle OpenRawHtml(string html, string title = "Cyréna");
}
```

### Methods

#### OpenUri(Uri uri, string title = "Cyréna")
Opens a URL in a new browser window/tab.

```csharp
IWindowHandle OpenUri(Uri uri, string title = "Cyréna");
```

#### OpenFile(string filePath, string title = "Cyréna")
Opens a local file path in a new browser window.

```csharp
IWindowHandle OpenFile(string filePath, string title = "Cyréna");
```

#### OpenRawHtml(string html, string title = "Cyréna")
Opens raw HTML content in a new browser window.

```csharp
IWindowHandle OpenRawHtml(string html, string title = "Cyréna");
```

### Return Value
All methods return `IWindowHandle` for window lifecycle management (close, dispose, event handling).

### Usage Example

```csharp
public class MyService
{
    private readonly IBrowserService _browser;

    public MyService(IBrowserService browser)
    {
        _browser = browser;
    }

    public void OpenDocumentation()
    {
        var handle = _browser.OpenUri(new Uri("https://docs.example.com"), "Documentation");
        handle.Closing += (s, e) => Console.WriteLine("Window closed");
    }

    public void OpenReport(string html)
    {
        var handle = _browser.OpenRawHtml(html, "Report");
        // ...
        handle.Close();
    }
}
```

